  "summary_md": "The furnishings batch lands in a weak housing demand backdrop, but the real standout is an unusual cluster of companies breaking out of the industry entirely. Several names are pivoting toward AI, critical minerals, and energy infrastructure: **ATER** abandoned its collapsed e-commerce model for tantalum trading and AI-driven exploration in Africa; **MWYN** and **XWIN** are chasing AI platform narratives despite thin cash runways and promotional framing; and **EFOI** is transforming from a niche lighting manufacturer into an Asia-focused data-center energy-storage play, backed by insider buying. Separately, **AMWD** grabs attention with its pending MasterBrand acquisition, carrying significant integration risk.\n\nElsewhere, traditional operators are hunkering down—**ETD**, **FLXS**, and **HOFT** lean on dividends and buybacks while managing choppy demand, and **SNBR** attempts a celebrity-fueled product reset amid deep skepticism. The batch splits sharply between steady cash-return stories and high-stakes reinventions.",
